      "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #60664.\n\nWhen structured output constraints (e.g. `response_format.json_schema`) are passed directly through the engine (via `LLM.generate`) rather than through the OpenAI serving layer, the grammar bitmask applies from token 0 — blocking the model's reasoning channel entirely.\n\n**Root cause:** `GptOssReasoningParser.is_reasoning_end()` always returns `True` (by design — the Harmony protocol uses structural tags to delineate reasoning). The OpenAI server wraps constraints in a structural tag via `HarmonyParser.adjust_request()`, but direct engine callers bypass this.\n\n**Fix:** Extract `to_harmony_structured_outputs()` from `_adjust_output_format()` in `vllm/parser/harmony.py`, then call it from `InputProcessor.process_inputs()` when the reasoning parser is `openai_gptoss` and `enable_in_reasoning` is off. This wraps plain constraints in the Harmony structural tag so the grammar only applies to the `<|channel|>final` section, preserving the `<|channel|>analysis` reasoning channel.\n\n- Requests that already carry a `structural_tag` are left as-is\n- Only activates when `reasoning_parser == \"openai_gptoss\"` and `enable_in_reasoning` is disabled\n- The existing OpenAI serving path is unchanged (refactored to use the same extracted function)\n\n## Test Results\n\n**Unit tests (CPU):** 7/7 custom tests passed — verifies `to_harmony_structured_outputs()` wraps json/regex/choice/json_object constraints in structural tags with the analysis channel prefix, and clears all original constraint fields.\n\n**GPU E2E tests (`openai/gpt-oss-20b`, 2x H100):** 9/9 passed\n- JSON schema response format: valid JSON with all required fields, 143 tokens in 1.39s, reasoning tracked (53 reasoning_tokens)\n- json_object response format: valid JSON output\n- Streaming + JSON schema: 120 SSE chunks, valid JSON\n- Baseline (no structured output): normal generation unaffected\n\n## Duplicate-work check\n\nPR #60678 addresses the same issue but has merge conflicts and a different approach. This PR takes a minimal approach scoped to the engine input processor.\n\n## AI Assistance\n\nThis change was developed with AI assistance (Claude). The submitter understands and can defend the change end-to-end.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
